&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2028 Point72 Academy Summer Internship — U.S.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a student interested in pursuing a career in investing? If you are graduating between December 2028 and July 2029, we invite you to apply for our 8-week summer internship, taking place from June to August 2028.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch your investing career in the Point72 Academy, an investment analyst training program designed to prepare you for a potential career on our fundamental equities teams.&amp;nbsp; Since 2015, the Academy has graduated more than 250 analysts onto our platform as of August 2026; some are portfolio managers today. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Point72 Academy Summer Internship combines structured training with real investing experience, including hands-on research on our investment teams. You’ll build the core skills used by public-markets investors and experience firsthand what it’s like to work as an Analyst at Point72. The internship can be your starting point into the full-time Point72 Academy Associate Program.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;During the internship, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a foundation in company research, financial analysis, and the skills needed to contribute as an investment analyst&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive training in accounting, modeling, presenting, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly on an investment team, gaining exposure to researching companies and industries alongside our analysts and portfolio managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn how investment ideas are developed, debated, and refined in a live market environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive feedback from Academy coaches as you dive deeper into data analysis and prepare a final investment pitch Explore efficient ways to harness AI in your investment processes and workflows in collaboration with Compliance, Information Security, and the Office of the Co-CIO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Point72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a firm that thrives on ideas, and we’ve found that the Point72 Academy has provided us with diverse viewpoints and perspectives, and we are able to offer support in their growth and development as analysts and portfolio managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;We welcome students from all academic disciplines. Your field of study or major is not a determining factor; we&#39;re looking for intellectual curiosity, integrity, strong judgment, and an interest in understanding businesses and markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want you to apply if you are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A current student who will graduate from university between December 2028 and July 2029.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fascinated by research, problem-solving, and analyzing how businesses work across different industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator who can develop a point of view and explain your thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to continued success in your academic and professional career with the highest levels of professionalism, integrity, and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-driven and motivated to explore a career in finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What to expect:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your online application, essays, and resume will serve as an introduction to who you are as a candidate. Once you complete the online application, we will begin reviewing your profile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selected candidates will then receive an email invitation to participate in a case study, allowing you to showcase your experiences and demonstrate your business acumen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Following submission and review of your case study, the next step would be an online assessment and virtual one on one interviews with various members of the Academy team, if selected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no set application deadline for this position. Candidates are considered as they apply, until the program is at capacity. We strongly encourage you to apply and fulfill all requirements as soon as you feel ready to begin the hiring process. Please note, you may only submit one application to the Academy internship program globally, so only apply to the region you are most interested in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t miss this opportunity to kickstart your career in the world of investing with the Point72 Academy. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary is $120,000 - $140,000 (USD) which will be prorated based on internship start and end date. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that any use of GenAI is strictly prohibited when completing this application.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A CAREER WITH POINT72’S ACADEMY TEAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Point72 Academy is the firm’s training program for fundamental equities financial analysts. Designed for undergraduates and early-career professionals, this immersive curriculum combines advanced modeling, critical thinking, and sector-specific research skills — preparing our analysts for an accelerated career trajectory at Point72.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Academy Recruiting team focuses on bringing to life the Point72 Academy’s mission, strategy, and initiatives. You will apply your experience in campus recruiting within competitive undergraduate programs to help evaluate candidates and identify the most promising future investment talent. Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain high-caliber pools of candidates—with a focus on undergrads and early-career professionals—and deliver effective initial screening to match prospective candidates with our opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support all aspects of global campus recruiting including sourcing, screening, and interviewing candidates to recommend top talent for entry to the Point72 Academy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Academy Management to determine strategic hiring plan for campus classes and review job descriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with Academy recruiting team, drive strategic university relationships, plan recruiting events and lead candidate debrief sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong relationships with potential candidates, universities and student organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enter and maintain data integrity and reporting in all applicable databases and ATS with strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with key business stakeholders to coordinate orientation and training for summer intern and early-career programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain apprised of current and changing recruiting methods through research and development of external network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in campus recruitment budget maintenance and analytical reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Corporate Communications and Compliance to curate and develop marketing messages and materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT’S REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of campus recruiting experience, with at least 3 in financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in applicant tracking systems and hiring platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills; confident engaging with candidates and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple recruiting campaigns under tight deadlines with sharp attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing campus strategies, building university partnerships, and supporting early career initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established network of talent acquisition professionals, university career services and other faculty, and student organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision-making skills: ability to track, analyze, and report recruiting metrics to assess effectiveness and optimize processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint; familiarity with HRIS/CRM and virtual recruiting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player with integrity, professionalism, and proactive problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstration of a high level of integrity, discretion and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel during peak campus recruiting seasons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE TAKE CARE OF OUR PEOPLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully-paid health care benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-profit matching gift program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, minorities and the LGBT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) savings program with an employer match and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://point72.com/&quot;&gt;https://point72.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $170,000-$200,000 (USD), which does not include discretionary bonus compensation or our comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring range based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PM Admin Assistant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are looking for an experienced administrative assistant to provide support to our portfolio managers and their team of research analysts.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Administrative Assistant, you will provide administrative support to one or several investment teams including portfolio managers and research analysts. Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically partner with investment team(s) to help alleviate workload and create efficiencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage calendars and conference calls, make appointments, book conference rooms, organize meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and process expense reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage phone coverage for team and set up conference calls as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in elements of the research process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform personal assistant functions (scheduling, reservations etc.) if required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify areas of improvement and develop solutions to help optimize team workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong working relationships with Brokers to manage corporate access for PM(s) and team in partnership with Compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research and aggregate data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow internal policies and due processes such as compliance approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on special projects as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s required &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong industry knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multitask and anticipate assignments while maintaining meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and organize earnings calls and conference dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive workflow management and strong communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to take on more responsibility and become an important member of team investment process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated sustained top performance as a PM administrative assistant, exemplifying our Mission, Value and Standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work autonomously with very little direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient level knowledge of Microsoft Outlook, Excel, and Word - Consistently lives Point72’s Mission and Values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
