&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The mission of Point72’s HR team is to be trusted strategic partners to the business, delivering data-driven people insights and operational excellence that enable informed decision-making and sustained performance. We leverage analytics, technology, and rigorous execution to support leaders and employees across the firm, while fostering a distinctive, inclusive culture grounded in collaboration, innovation, and integrity. Through thoughtful use of data and insight, we help attract, develop, and retain exceptional talent at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Act as the primary HR operations contact, responding to employee questions on HR policies, benefits, and standard procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Manage the full employee lifecycle, including onboarding, internal moves, role changes, leaves of absence, and offboarding.&lt;br&gt;• Prepare, process, and maintain employee contracts, amendments, and HR documentation in coordination with HRBPs, Legal, Payroll, and vendors.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain accurate employee and benefits data across HR systems, ensuring consistency between HRIS, Payroll, and benefits providers.&lt;br&gt;• Perform regular data checks, reconciliations, and audits to ensure accuracy, compliance, and data integrity.&lt;br&gt;• Partner with global HR Business Partners to support day to day HR execution, allowing them to focus on strategic initiatives.&lt;br&gt;• Produce recurring and ad hoc HR reports such as headcount, attrition, hiring, mobility, and workforce demographics.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain and improve standardized HR dashboards, trackers, and reporting tools for HR leadership and stakeholders while ensuring data integrity.&lt;br&gt;• Support internal and external audits, regulatory reporting, and workforce data requests.&lt;br&gt;• Identify trends, gaps, and inefficiencies in HR data and processes, and contribute to continuous improvement, standardization, and automation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WHAT’S REQUIRED&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Relevant experience in an HR Analyst or HR operations role&lt;br&gt;• Experience working with HRIS platforms and HR data management systems&lt;br&gt;• Strong analytical skills with advanced proficiency in Excel and PowerPoint; experience with Power BI or similar data visualization tools preferred&lt;br&gt;• Ability to thrive in a fast-paced financial services environment&lt;br&gt;• Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated ability to handle confidential information with professionalism and discretion&lt;br&gt;• Strong organizational skills with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple responsibilities&lt;br&gt;• Team-oriented mindset with strong collaboration skills&lt;br&gt;• High attention to detail&lt;br&gt;• Commitment to the highest ethical and professional standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WE TAKE CARE OF OUR PEOPLE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;br&gt;• Health care benefits&lt;br&gt;• Maternity, Adoption &amp;amp; related leave policies&lt;br&gt;• Generous paternity and family care leave policies&lt;br&gt;• Employee Assistance Program &amp;amp; Mental wellness programs&lt;br&gt;• Transportation support&lt;br&gt;• Tuition assistance&lt;/p&gt;
