&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Identity &amp;amp; Privileged Governance Analyst to join our Information Security team, supporting identity and privileged access governance, monitoring, and remediation initiatives across the firm. Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support identity and privileged access governance, hygiene, and remediation activities, with a focus on service account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor identity and privileged access controls, identify gaps, risks, and exceptions, and drive remediation to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and enforce identity and privileged access policies, standards, and control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and facilitate working sessions to deliver remediation, audit, and control initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with application, engineering, and platform teams to map and govern access models within the firm’s Identity Governance &amp;amp; Administration solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and respond to identity and privileged access requests and inquiries via shared mailboxes and ticketing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate IAM and PAM requirements, standards, and expectations effectively to technical and non‑technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate, audit‑ready documentation for IAM/PAM processes, access decisions, remediation activities, and control evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools and LLMs to automate repeatable tasks and improve efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular status updates and contribute to IAM/PAM program maturity by identifying trends, risks, and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in information security, IAM, PAM, or a related technology risk discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of IAM and PAM concepts, controls, and risks, including service accounts and privileged credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands‑on experience with PAM solutions (e.g., CyberArk or similar), Active Directory, privileged access models, and identity lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting access remediation initiatives, control improvements, and governance efforts in an enterprise environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity and privileged access policies, standards, and control frameworks, including audit support (evidence gathering, validation, and remediation tracking).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to partner effectively with application, engineering, and platform teams to understand and govern access‑related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools and LLMs (e.g., Claude or similar) to automate operational tasks and support IAM/PAM governance and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, documentation, and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple workstreams and deliver audit‑ready outputs on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
