&lt;p&gt;Manager, International Communications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72’s Corporate Communications team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Communications team manages the global reputation of Point72 and all related entities. The team is responsible for all aspects of corporate communications, including media relations, executive visibility and thought leadership, internal communications, digital content and distribution, and brand management. As a small, collaborative team, we work closely with senior management and colleagues across the organization to communicate the firm’s priorities, support key business initiatives, and retain and attract the industry’s brightest talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in London, you’ll lead Point72’s corporate communications across EMEA and APAC. Working closely with the U.S.-based Co-Heads of Corporate Communications and regional business leaders, you’ll develop and execute communications strategies that reflect regional needs while advancing the firm’s global priorities. The role combines strategic counsel to senior leaders with hands-on responsibility for media relations, executive visibility, internal communications, and regional agency management. This includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate closely with the broader Corporate Communications team&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure communications strategies and messaging are consistent across regions and aligned with the firm’s global priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead media relations across EMEA and APAC&lt;/strong&gt;, build relationships with key reporters, and serve as a spokesperson for the firm. Provide media training and coaching to regional executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead internal communications across international offices&lt;/strong&gt;, helping to strengthen the firm’s culture and keep employees connected and informed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advise regional business leaders on communications priorities&lt;/strong&gt; and strategic initiatives working closely with the U.S.-based Corporate Communications team to align regional communications with the firm’s global priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify and pursue executive visibility and thought leadership opportunities&lt;/strong&gt; for regional leaders and the economist team, including media interviews, and speaking engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with regional recruiting teams&lt;/strong&gt; to develop messaging, content, and branded materials that reflect the firm&#39;s culture and support talent attraction and employee engagement across EMEA and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage regional communications agency partners&lt;/strong&gt;, setting priorities, guiding execution, and ensuring their work meets the firm’s standards and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visit international offices regularly&lt;/strong&gt; to build relationships with key media contacts, as well as strengthen relationships internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an external communications professional with strong media relations expertise and an interest in broadening their experience across the communications function. The ideal candidate will combine strategic thinking with a hands-on approach and exercise sound judgment. They should be comfortable operating with ambiguity, adapting to changing priorities, and working independently while staying closely connected to the broader team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least seven years of communications experience in-house, at an agency, or in the public sector, including experience in financial services or advising financial services clients, with a strong understanding of the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive mindset and ability to move fluidly between strategic counsel and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
